<body>
    <h1>Curated - Logging &amp; Reconciliation</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>The primary purpose of Logging &amp; Reconciliation is to check =
that the data fed into a process comes out of the other side and has not be=
en inadvertently altered.&nbsp;This can also be a useful tool during develo=
pment and testing providing assurance that processes have completed to a ce=
rtain degree of success but it is not a substitute for unit or system testi=
ng.</p>
<p>
 <style type=3D"text/css">/*<![CDATA[*/
div.rbtoc1769450194329 {padding: 0px;}
div.rbtoc1769450194329 ul {margin-left: 0px;}
div.rbtoc1769450194329 li {margin-left: 0px;padding-left: 0px;}

/*]]>*/</style></p>
<div class=3D"toc-macro rbtoc1769450194329">
 <ul class=3D"toc-indentation">
  <li><a href=3D"#CuratedLogging&amp;Reconciliation-LoggingPoint">Logging P=
oint</a></li>
  <li><a href=3D"#CuratedLogging&amp;Reconciliation-ReconciliationPoint">Re=
conciliation Point</a></li>
  <li><a href=3D"#CuratedLogging&amp;Reconciliation-Configuration">Configur=
ation</a></li>
  <li><a href=3D"#CuratedLogging&amp;Reconciliation-Execution">Execution</a=
></li>
  <li><a href=3D"#CuratedLogging&amp;Reconciliation-QueryingResults">Queryi=
ng Results</a></li>
 </ul>
</div>
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"CuratedLogging&amp;Reconciliation-LoggingPoint"><strong>Logging P=
oint</strong></h2>
<p>A Logging Point is a point in a process where counts can be taken for th=
e purpose of data reconciliation. A Logging Point outputs a numeric result =
based on a view, this view will generally be made up of a number of sub-que=
ries.</p>
<p>Below is an example Logging Point view that compares Flow Policy Vehicle=
 data loaded to the EDW (Data Vault) vs the source data held in the ODS. Ea=
ch Logging Point will normally reconcile the data across multiple tables i.=
e. across a subset of the data model.</p>
<ul>
 <li><strong>w_dv</strong>: a query across the Data Vault, business identif=
iers and main timestamps returned as columns with a HASH of the remaining c=
olumns to compare. A HASH is used as it was found to be the best way to con=
sistently handle differences in data types. A NOT EXISTS sub-query is used =
to exclude cases with known issues.</li>
 <li><strong>w_srce</strong>:&nbsp;a query across the Source data with the =
same structure as w_dv.&nbsp;A NOT EXISTS sub-query is used to exclude case=
s with known issues.</li>
 <li><strong>w_srce_dv_except</strong>: a comparison (EXCEPT) of the data i=
n the Source to that in the Data Vault.</li>
 <li><strong>w_srce_dv</strong>: a COUNT of the differences identified in w=
_srce_dv_except.</li>
 <li><strong>w_dv_srce_except</strong>: a comparison (EXCEPT) of the data i=
n the Data Vault to that in the Source.</li>
 <li><strong>w_dv_srce</strong>:&nbsp;a COUNT of the differences identified=
 in w_dv_srce_except.</li>
 <li><strong>w_row_count_match</strong>: a comparison (EXCEPT) of the row C=
OUNT of the data in the Data Vault vs Source.</li>
 <li><strong>LOGGED_CNT</strong>: the final result calculated by adding the=
 above COUNTs. The standard approach is to expect the Logging Point to retu=
rn 0 if the data matches across the Data Vault and Source.<br><br></li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: sql; gutter: false">CREATE VIEW dwh_audit.vw_ins_lp_flow_policy_vehicle=
_to_edw
AS=20
WITH w_dv
AS
(
 -- -----------------------------------------------------------------------=
-----
 -- -----------------------------------------------------------------------=
-----
 -- View: VW_INS_LP_FLOW_POLICY_VEHICLE_TO_EDW
 --
 -- EDW Flow logic to evaluate a logging point to reconcile Flow Policy Veh=
icle
 -- data.
 --
 -- REVISIONS:
 -- Sprint     Date Time         Author               Description
 -----------   ----------------  -------------------  ---------------------=
-----
 -- 10.2       07/08/2020 14:30  S Fisher             Change to make Email =
Address consistent
 --                                                   across all objects, i=
ncluding adding of
 --                                                   TRIM.
 -- -----------------------------------------------------------------------=
-----
 -- -----------------------------------------------------------------------=
-----
 SELECT ph.policy_number_ref
       ,pvfs.policy_version_number
       ,pvfs.policy_version_issue_date
       ,pvfs.policy_version_start_date
       ,CONVERT(BINARY(20),HASHBYTES('SHA1',CONCAT(pvfs.policy_version_id,'=
^'
                                                  ,CONVERT(DATETIME2(3),pvf=
s.policy_version_end_date),'^'
                                                  ,pvfs.policy_version_stat=
us_code,'^'
                                                  ,pvfs.policy_version_stat=
us_text,'^'
                                                  ,pvfs.interaction_id,'^'
                                                  ,pvfs.product_model_versi=
on,'^'
                                                  ,viol.vrn_ref,'^'
                                                  ,viofs.object_id,'^'
                                                  ,viofs.vin,'^'
                                                  ,viofs.year,'^'
                                                  ,CONVERT(DATETIME2(3),vio=
fs.first_registration_date),'^'
                                                  ,viofs.make,'^'
                                                  ,viofs.model,'^'
                                                  ,viofs.variant,'^'
                                                  --,peh.plhdr_email_addres=
s_ref,'^'
                                                  ,ISNULL(peh.plhdr_email_a=
ddress_ref,'(?)'),'^'
                                                  ,pfs.reference_number,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.party_type_code,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.party_type_text,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.name,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.first_name,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.last_name,'^'
                                                  ,CONVERT(DATETIME2(3),pfs=
.date_of_birth),'^'
                                                  ,pfs.address_line1,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.address_line2,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.address_line3,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.address_line4,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.postal_code,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.town,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.county,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.country,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.phone_mobile,'^'
                                                  ,pfs.phone_landline,'^'))=
) AS hash_diff
 FROM curated_edw.policy_hub ph
 INNER JOIN curated_edw.policy_version_flw_sat pvfs  ON (pvfs.policy_key   =
                   =3D ph.policy_key)
 -- POLICYHOLDER
 INNER JOIN curated_edw.plhdr_email_lnk pel          ON (pel.policy_key    =
                   =3D ph.policy_key)
 INNER JOIN curated_edw.plhdr_email_hub peh          ON (peh.plhdr_email_ke=
y                  =3D pel.plhdr_email_key
                                                         -- Business Key jo=
in to check data matches only.
                                                     AND peh.plhdr_email_ad=
dress_ref           =3D pel.plhdr_email_address_ref)
 INNER JOIN curated_edw.plhdr_flw_sat pfs            ON (pfs.plhdr_email_ke=
y                   =3D peh.plhdr_email_key
                                                     AND  pvfs.policy_versi=
on_issue_date BETWEEN pfs.sys_efctv_dt   AND pfs.sys_exptn_dt
                                                     AND  pvfs.policy_versi=
on_start_date BETWEEN pfs.busns_efctv_dt AND pfs.busns_exptn_dt)=20
 -- INSURED_OBJECT_VEHICLE
 INNER JOIN curated_edw.veh_ins_obj_lnk viol         ON (viol.policy_key   =
                    =3D ph.policy_key)
 INNER JOIN curated_edw.veh_ins_obj_efctvy_sat vioes ON (vioes.veh_ins_obj_=
lnk_key             =3D viol.veh_ins_obj_lnk_key
                                                     AND  pvfs.policy_versi=
on_issue_date BETWEEN vioes.sys_efctv_dt   AND vioes.sys_exptn_dt
                                                     AND  pvfs.policy_versi=
on_start_date BETWEEN vioes.busns_efctv_dt AND vioes.busns_exptn_dt)=20
 INNER JOIN curated_edw.veh_ins_obj_flw_sat viofs    ON (viofs.veh_ins_obj_=
lnk_key             =3D viol.veh_ins_obj_lnk_key
                                                     AND pvfs.policy_versio=
n_issue_date  BETWEEN viofs.sys_efctv_dt   AND viofs.sys_exptn_dt
                                                     AND pvfs.policy_versio=
n_start_date  BETWEEN viofs.busns_efctv_dt AND viofs.busns_exptn_dt)=20
 INNER JOIN curated_edw.veh_vrn_hub vvh              ON (vvh.veh_vrn_key   =
                    =3D viol.veh_vrn_key
                                                         -- Business Key jo=
in to check data matches only.
                                                     AND vvh.vrn_ref       =
                    =3D viol.vrn_ref)
 WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1
                   FROM   dwh_audit.dwh_logging_point dlp
                   LEFT JOIN dwh_audit.dwh_logging_point_excln dlpe ON (dlp=
e.logging_point_id =3D dlp.logging_point_id)
                   WHERE  dlp.logging_point_name =3D 'LP_FLOW_POLICY_VEHICL=
E_TO_EDW'
                   AND    dlpe.policy_number_ref =3D ph.policy_number_ref
                   AND    dlpe.sys_efctv_dt      =3D pvfs.sys_efctv_dt
                   AND    dlpe.busns_efctv_dt    =3D pvfs.busns_efctv_dt
                   AND    dlpe.active_ind        =3D 'Y')
)
,w_srce
AS
(
 SELECT p.policy_number
       ,pv.policy_version_number
       ,CONVERT(DATETIME2(3),pv.issue_date) AS issue_date
       ,CONVERT(DATETIME2(3),pv.start_date) AS start_date
       ,CONVERT(BINARY(20),HASHBYTES('SHA1',CONCAT(pv.policy_version_id,'^'
                                                  ,CONVERT(DATETIME2(3),pv.=
end_date),'^'
                                                  ,epvs.policy_version_stat=
us_code,'^'
                                                  ,epvs.policy_version_stat=
us_text,'^'
                                                  ,pv.interaction_id,'^'
                                                  ,pp.product_model_version=
,'^'
                                                  ,ISNULL(REPLACE(UPPER(oc.=
registration_number),' ',''),'(?)'),'^'
                                                  ,oc.object_id,'^'
                                                  ,oc.vin,'^'
                                                  ,oc.year,'^'
                                                  ,CONVERT(DATETIME2(3),oc.=
first_registration_date),'^'
                                                  ,oc.make,'^'
                                                  ,oc.model,'^'
                                                  ,oc.variant,'^'
                                                  ,ISNULL(TRIM(LOWER(CASE W=
HEN pa.email =3D ''=20
                                                                          T=
HEN NULL=20
                                                                          E=
LSE pa.email
                                                                     END)),=
'(?)'),'^'
                                                  ,pa.reference_number,'^'
                                                  ,ept.party_type_code,'^'
                                                  ,ept.party_type_text,'^'
                                                  ,pa.name,'^'
                                                  ,pa.first_name,'^'
                                                  ,pa.last_name,'^'
                                                  ,CONVERT(DATETIME2(3),pa.=
date_of_birth),'^'
                                                  ,pa.address_line1,'^'
                                                  ,pa.address_line2,'^'
                                                  ,pa.address_line3,'^'
                                                  ,pa.address_line4,'^'
                                                  ,pa.postal_code,'^'
                                                  ,pa.town,'^'
                                                  ,pa.county,'^'
                                                  ,pa.country,'^'
                                                  ,pa.phone_mobile,'^'
                                                  ,pa.phone_landline,'^')))=
 AS hash_diff
 FROM   flow_policyadmin.lnd_current_change_ext_policy p
 INNER JOIN flow_policyadmin.lnd_current_change_ext_policy_version pv      =
         ON (pv.policy_id                  =3D p.policy_id)
 INNER JOIN flow_policyadmin.lnd_current_change_ext_enum_policy_version_sta=
tus epvs ON (epvs.policy_version_status_id =3D pv.policy_version_status_id)
 LEFT JOIN flow_policyadmin.lnd_current_change_ext_party pa                =
        ON (pa.party_id                   =3D p.party_id)
 LEFT JOIN  flow_policyadmin.lnd_current_change_ext_enum_party_type ept    =
         ON (ept.party_type_id             =3D pa.party_type_id)
 INNER JOIN flow_policyadmin.lnd_current_change_ext_product_package pp     =
         ON (pp.policy_version_id          =3D pv.policy_version_id)
 INNER JOIN flow_policyadmin.lnd_current_change_ext_object o               =
         ON (o.product_package_id          =3D pp.product_package_id)
 INNER JOIN flow_policyadmin.lnd_current_change_ext_object_car oc          =
         ON (oc.object_id                  =3D o.object_id)
 WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1
                   FROM   dwh_audit.dwh_logging_point dlp
                   LEFT JOIN dwh_audit.dwh_logging_point_excln dlpe ON (dlp=
e.logging_point_id =3D dlp.logging_point_id)
                   WHERE  dlp.logging_point_name =3D 'LP_FLOW_POLICY_VEHICL=
E_TO_EDW'
                   AND    dlpe.policy_number_ref =3D p.policy_number
                   AND    dlpe.sys_efctv_dt      =3D CONVERT(DATETIME2(3),p=
v.issue_date)
                   AND    dlpe.busns_efctv_dt    =3D CONVERT(DATETIME2(3),p=
v.start_date)
                   AND    dlpe.active_ind        =3D 'Y')
)
,w_srce_dv_except
AS
(
 SELECT *
 FROM   w_srce
 EXCEPT
 SELECT *
 FROM   w_dv
)
,w_srce_dv
AS
(
 SELECT COUNT(*) AS w_srce_dv_cnt
 FROM   w_srce_dv_except
)
,w_dv_srce_except
AS
(
 SELECT *
 FROM   w_dv
 EXCEPT
 SELECT *
 FROM   w_srce
)
,w_dv_srce
AS
(
 SELECT COUNT(*) AS w_dv_srce_cnt
 FROM   w_dv_srce_except
)
,w_row_count_match
AS
(
 SELECT COUNT(*) AS w_row_cnt
 FROM   (
         SELECT COUNT(*) AS w_dv_row_cnt FROM w_dv
         EXCEPT
         SELECT COUNT(*) AS w_srce_row_cnt FROM w_srce
        ) iv_row_cnt
)
SELECT lp.LOGGING_POINT_ID
      ,w_srce_dv_cnt + w_dv_srce_cnt + w_row_cnt AS LOGGED_CNT=20
FROM   w_srce_dv
     , w_dv_srce
     , w_row_count_match
     , (SELECT logging_point_id
        FROM   dwh_audit.dwh_logging_point
        WHERE  logging_point_name =3D 'LP_FLOW_POLICY_VEHICLE_TO_EDW') lp</=
pre>
 </div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"CuratedLogging&amp;Reconciliation-ReconciliationPoint"><strong st=
yle=3D"font-size: 20.0px;letter-spacing: -0.008em;">Reconciliation Point</s=
trong></h2>
<p>A Reconciliation Point defines a point in a process where logged data co=
unts are summed and compared to an expected value to ensure that all data h=
as been processed and accounted for and there have been no unusual data mov=
ements.&nbsp; It consists of a configuration of one or more Logging Points =
that on collation produce a&nbsp;SUCCESS or FAILURE result.</p>
<h2 id=3D"CuratedLogging&amp;Reconciliation-Configuration"><strong style=3D=
"font-size: 20.0px;letter-spacing: -0.008em;">Configuration</strong></h2>
<p>The Data Warehouse Audit schema holds the data model used to configure L=
ogging and Reconciliation points.</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper"><img class=3D"confluenc=
e-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" src=3D"beb564fa787c04ed8d5b4529de1e92=
